WEBVTT

00:00:00.482 --> 00:00:05.152
PostgreSQL has an optional crosstab function through the tablefunc extension.

00:00:05.152 --> 00:00:11.552
It can create pivot tables, but it requires extension support and explicit output-column definitions.

00:00:11.552 --> 00:00:16.517
For this course, conditional aggregation is the core pattern because it is transparent and works well in the

00:00:16.517 --> 00:00:22.987
browser environment. You can explore crosstab later for selected reporting scenarios.

00:00:22.987 --> 00:00:27.567
Static pivots are easier to read and validate when the category set is known.

00:00:27.567 --> 00:00:30.927
Dynamic pivots are useful when categories change,

00:00:30.927 --> 00:00:36.087
but they introduce schema variability that downstream dashboards or models must handle.

00:00:36.087 --> 00:00:41.109
Discover categories first and decide whether a changing column set is acceptable.
